# Mandatory Calendar Follow-Ups — NON-NEGOTIABLE

**Every outbound action gets a follow-up on the calendar. No exceptions. No "I'll remember." No relying on Dee to ask.**

## The Rule

When ANY of the following actions occur, NEXUS MUST create a calendar event for the follow-up:

### Buyer/CO Outreach Emails
- **Follow-up event:** 7 days after send date
- **Title format:** `FOLLOW UP — [CO Name], [Agency] — [Purpose]`
- **Second follow-up:** 14 days if no response to first
- **Third follow-up:** 21 days — final touch, then mark "No Response — Revisit 60 days"

### Pre-Bid Conferences / Zoom Meetings
- **Day-of reminder:** Calendar event on the day/time of the meeting
- **Follow-up event:** 2 business days after — check for addenda, notes, contact the CO if needed

### Bid Submission Deadlines
- **7-day warning:** Calendar event 7 days before deadline
- **3-day warning:** Calendar event 3 days before deadline
- **Day-of reminder:** Calendar event on deadline day, 2 hours before due time

### Questions Submitted to COs
- **Follow-up event:** 5 business days after submission — check for posted answers

### Subcontractor / Supplier Outreach
- **Follow-up event:** 3 business days after send
- **Second follow-up:** 7 days if no response

### SWFT / Clearance / Registration Applications
- **Follow-up event:** 10 business days after submission
- **Recurring check:** Every 2 weeks until resolved

## Calendar Event Requirements

Every follow-up calendar event MUST include:
- **Who** to contact (name + email in the location field)
- **What** the follow-up is about (reference solicitation # or topic)
- **What to do** if no response (escalation step in the description)

## When This Triggers

- When generating a SEND_TO_BUYER email → create follow-up event
- When logging a CO outreach email as sent → create follow-up event
- When a pre-bid conference is identified → create day-of event + post-conference follow-up
- When a bid deadline is identified → create 7-day, 3-day, and day-of reminders
- When questions are submitted → create answer-check event
- When any application/registration is submitted → create follow-up event

## No Exceptions

This is not optional. This is not "when convenient." Every action gets a follow-up. The calendar is the safety net. If it's not on the calendar, it doesn't exist.

**Missing the Fulton County pre-bid conference is why this rule exists. Never again.**
